# How far this agent sits from what it wants — the diff between the desired and the sensed
# state, one row per property it holds a region in AND has an observation of.
#
# This is the question the whole capability exists to make askable, so it is SPARQL the package
# ships rather than arithmetic inside the module: metrics reports it, a review may cite it, and
# a reader with nothing but a SPARQL client can ask it of any store. The module's own `urgency`
# is held to agreeing with it by the package's tests — one definition, two readers.
#
# `$me` and `$sensed` are the two things a shipped query cannot know and are substituted before
# it runs, exactly as a `review.rq`'s placeholders are: the one instance identifier a process is
# given, and the graph its own observations land in. Everything else is discovered, and the
# region patterns are deliberately UNQUALIFIED — desire is a class of graph so a second source
# must be readable, and the trap AGENTS.md names (a GRAPH clause silently matching nothing) is
# exactly what an unqualified pattern avoids.
#
# THE NUMBER: signed, and normalised by the survival room on the side the value sits on.
#
#     gap = (value - centre) / |outer(side) - centre|,   clamped to [-1, 1]
#
# where `outer` is the survival bound on that side when the world states one and the region's
# own edge when it does not. So 0 is the point of the region, the sign says which way out
# (negative = below, toward LOW), and |gap| = 1 means the edge of what the subject survives —
# |gap| is the module's `urgency`, by construction rather than by coincidence. A region with no
# width and no envelope is all-or-nothing: 0 at its point, ±1 anywhere else.
#
# A property with no observation yet produces NO row rather than a zero — at birth every desire
# is unmeasured, and "unmeasured" must not read as "satisfied". The first intention is always
# to look; see knowledge/decisions/an-intention-is-an-amortised-deliberation.md.
#
# ?at is WHEN the sensed side was measured, carried so a reader can refuse a stale row. The
# refusing itself is deliberately not here: how old is too old is the agent's own freshness
# rule — the cadence it commanded plus its grace, per sensor, per property — and a shipped
# query cannot know a policy that moves with the cadence. The query answers what the diff IS
# and when each side was true; whoever consumes it judges. See issue #124.

SELECT ?property ?value ?low ?high ?gap ?at WHERE {
  $me ag:holds ?region ; ag:actsFor ?subject .
  ?region ssn:forProperty ?property ; sh:property ?want .
  ?want sh:severity ag:ShouldBecome ;
        sh:qualifiedValueShape/sh:property/sh:minInclusive ?low ;
        sh:qualifiedValueShape/sh:property/sh:maxInclusive ?high .
  OPTIONAL { $me ag:holds ?envelope .
             ?envelope ssn:forProperty ?property ; sh:property ?tolerate .
             ?tolerate sh:severity sh:Warning ;
                       sh:qualifiedValueShape/sh:not/sh:property/sh:minInclusive ?floor ;
                       sh:qualifiedValueShape/sh:not/sh:property/sh:maxInclusive ?ceiling }
  GRAPH $sensed {
    ?obs sosa:hasFeatureOfInterest ?subject ;
         sosa:observedProperty ?property ;
         sosa:hasSimpleResult ?value .
    OPTIONAL { ?obs sosa:resultTime ?at }
  }
  BIND((?low + ?high) / 2 AS ?centre)
  BIND(IF(?value < ?centre, COALESCE(?floor, ?low), COALESCE(?ceiling, ?high)) AS ?outer)
  BIND(IF(?outer > ?centre, ?outer - ?centre, ?centre - ?outer) AS ?room)
  #  ?value = ?centre is short-circuited BEFORE the division, and not only for elegance:
  #  this store's engine (pyoxigraph, measured on 0.4.x) errors on decimal division when the
  #  DIVIDEND is zero — 0.2/0.3 binds, 0/0.3 does not — so the row for a perfectly content
  #  agent silently lost its ?gap and gaps_of raised. Found the day the sovereign channel's
  #  test seeded a reading exactly at fern's centre; every earlier test happened to sit
  #  off-centre. The zero case is answered by arithmetic nobody disputes: at the centre, the
  #  gap is 0.
  BIND(IF(?value = ?centre, 0.0,
          IF(?room = 0, IF(?value > ?centre, 1.0, -1.0),
             (?value - ?centre) / ?room)) AS ?raw)
  BIND(IF(?raw > 1, 1.0, IF(?raw < -1, -1.0, ?raw)) AS ?gap)
}
ORDER BY ?property
